%---------------- ISPF Tutorial 4 of 5: Actions --------------------------%
%Command ===>_ZCMD
+
 Action commands take the row number shown in the current filtered and
 sorted list. For example, BROWSE 3 acts on result 3, not necessarily
 the third row of the complete catalog listing.
+
 BROWSE, EDIT, and VIEW call the corresponding ISPF services. INFO
 reports the volume, size, device, and migration indicator returned by
 LMDLIST. Use the main panel's displayed row order when choosing a row.
+
 ULS intentionally excludes delete, rename, copy, move, and allocation
 commands. Those operations can change catalog contents and require
 additional installation-specific validation.
+
 Enter NEXT, PREV, 1-5, or END to navigate.
)END
